    "description": "Mixed Mineral Specimen & Gemstone Lot\nNatural & Polished Stones\nLot of Various Specimens\nThis diverse collection features a variety of natural mineral specimens, rough crystal formations, fossils, and polished tumbled stones. Notable pieces include a vibrant golden-brown citrine crystal cluster, a pinkish-brown aragonite sputnik formation, a banded agate geode section, a knapped chert projectile point, and a fossilized bivalve shell specimen. The lot also includes an assortment of smooth polished pocket stones, including quartz pebbles, jasper, and a specialty tumbled stone featuring an etched black paw print design.\nVariety of natural crystal formations, fossils, and polished stones\nFeatures citrine cluster, aragonite star, banded agate, and fossil specimen\nIncludes knapped stone arrowhead and decorative paw print tumbled pebble\nSuitable for mineral collectors, lapidary projects, decor, or educational study\nCondition:\nOverall very good pre-owned condition across the collection. Natural specimens exhibit organic variations, crystalline textures, and matrix characteristics typical of raw minerals. Polished stones show smooth tumbled finishes with light handling wear. Projectile point displays intact knapped edges. Sold as a complete assorted lot as pictured.",
